+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(|M|)$ where $|M|$ is the number of slots in the hash table [S1].
+*   **Performance:** Constant-time lookups support real-time rendering. Limiting ejection depth reduces thread divergence in GPU implementations [S1].
+*   **Strengths:** Constant-time lookup and reduced thread divergence compared to full Cuckoo hashing [S1].
+*   **Limitations:** Higher miss rate than standard Cuckoo hashing due to element removal when collision chains cannot be resolved within the depth limit [S1].
 
 ## Background
-The method originates from the paper "Random Access Segmentation Volume Compression for Interactive Volume Rendering" [S1]. It is designed to support interactive volume rendering by caching voxel labels, which are used to determine visibility and transfer function application. The adaptation of Cuckoo hashing is specifically tailored for the constraints of GPU rendering, such as thread divergence and the need for constant-time operations [S1].
